[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Heracles External GUI SW Verification Test Protocol
UID: DHF-HRC-0047-TP
METADATA:
  COMPONENT: heracles-external-gui

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @grammar

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Purpose

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
This document provides the verification test protocol and execution results of the External GUI SW for the Heracles system. It defines the test cases that are used to verify the compliance of the software with the Heracles External GUI SW Verification Plan and Software Requirements Specification.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Scope

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
This document details all regression test cases for the Verification testing activities of Heracles External GUI Software. Each test case is designed to verify specific functional, interface, and usability requirements of the system, including treatment control, quality assurance, and operational workflows.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Abbreviations and Definitions

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
FW
Firmware

SDP
Software Development Plan

SVP
Software Verification Plan

SW
Software

GUI
Graphical User Interface

QA
Quality Assurance

DB
Database

GCB
Grid Control Board

HVPS
High Voltage Power Supply

MCU
Microcontroller Unit

LED
Light Emitting Diode

PID
Proportional Integral Derivative
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: References

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Heracles SDP - DHF-HRC-0001 Rev. 2

Heracles SVP - DHF-HRC-0003 Rev. 2

Heracles External GUI SRS - DHF-HRC-0007 Rev. 3

Heracles Software Architecture Description - DHF-HRC-0004 Rev. 2

Heracles External GUI Verification Protocol - DHF-HRC-0047 Rev. 2

Heracles External GUI Verification Execution Report - DHF-HRC-0048 Rev. 2
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
PREFIX: TC-H10TG-
TITLE: Test Cases

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H10TG-58
TITLE: Treatment Console - Radiation Emission Control - Prepare process - Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
Verify the user interface layout of the application accurately reflects the system's status and button labels during the treatment preparation process.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
Load a plan for treatment in the Heracles Internal unit.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Log in to the External application. 

2. Navigate to the treatment view. 

3. Press the Prepare button to prepare the treatment.
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1 - The interface should display the following states: 

System status: COLD 

Button Label: Prepare 

3 - The interface should display the following states: 

System status: WARMUP 

Button's label: Warming up ( with progress bar) 

then System status: HVSetup ( On Loading) 

Upon completion of the preparation process: 

System status: READY
<<<

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H10TG-121
TITLE: Quality Assurance - Daily Warmup
STATEMENT: >>>
This test case verifies quality assurance checks and validations. It ensures that the system properly executes quality control procedures.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Log in to the External application. 

2. Navigate to the Startup Cycle tab in the Quality Assurance view. 

3. Press Warmup.
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
3 - The warmup process is performed, and a new record is added to the warmup report.
<<<

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H10TG-62
TITLE: Radiation Emission Control - Emission Error Indicator - Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
This test case aims to verify the application displays a visible indicator for an emission error in the system.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
1)Load a plan for treatment in the Heracles Internal unit.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Log in to the External application. 

2. Navigate to the treatment view. 

3. Press the Prepare button to prepare the treatment. 

4. Press the Beam-On button to trigger emission delivery 

5. 

.Introduce a deliberate error in the firmware (e.g., trigger an e-stop interlock) .
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
A visible indicator is displayed to indicate a system error.
<<<

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H10TG-98
TITLE: Treatment View - Patient Details - Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
This test case aims to verify that the treatment console displays details about the treated patient and its treated site. The patient details shall include the following: • Patient's full name • MRN • Patient DOB • Field Name • Dose to be delivered • Applicator Size • Field/Shield Size • Devices • Setup Notes ( Simulation notes)
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
Load a plan for treatment from the internal unit.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1.Launch Heracles External 

2.Click the Treatment tab
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
The treatment console shall display details about the treated patient and its treated site. 

The patient details shall includes all required data
<<<

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H10TG-101
TITLE: Treatment View - Telemetry - No communication to GCB indication - (UI) Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
This test case aims to verify that the telemetry controls provide a clear indication when there is no communication with the GCB.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
Load a plan for treatment in Heracles Internal unit 

This test case requires the capability to generate a communication error with the GCB
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1.Launch Heracles External 

2.Click the Treatment tab 

3.Generate a deliberate communication error with the GCB
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
The telemetry controls shall provide a clear indication that there is no communication with the GCB. 

The System Status shall show - NO-COMM 

Timers, Energy, and Current shall show - ~0 ( around 0)
<<<

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H10TG-114
TITLE: Quality Assurance - Daily Warmup - Error Indicator
STATEMENT: >>>
This test case verifies the handling of errors and faults in the system. It ensures appropriate responses to error conditions.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Log in to the External application. 

2. Navigate to the Startup Cycle tab in the Quality Assurance view. 

3. Press Warmup. 

4. 

Simulate error ( i.e. activate interlock)
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
4 - Error indicator should be displayed on the view, and the user can click on it and see the error.
<<<

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H10TG-295
TITLE: Resume Uncompleted Treatment Alert
STATEMENT: >>>
This test case verifies that the application alerts the operator if the loaded plan was not completely delivered and enables the operator to choose to deliver the remaining plan.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
Load a plan for treatment in the Heracles Internal unit.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Log in to the External application. 

2. Navigate to the treatment view. 

3. Press the Prepare button to prepare the treatment. 

4. Press the Beam-On button to trigger emission delivery. 

5. Press the stop button 

6. Unload the plan 

7. Log in to the Internal application. 

8. Navigate to the treatment view. 

9. Load the plan into the external application. 

10. Go to the External application. 

11. Press the Prepare button to prepare the treatment.
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
5 - The emission process should be stopped, and the status should become primed. 

6 - The plan should be unloaded and removed from the UI. 

11 - An alert message should be displayed informing the user that the treatment was not delivered completely and it will resume the 
emission for the remaining time.
<<<

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H10TG-131
TITLE: Treatment View - Alert for uncompleted Daily Safety checks - 2
STATEMENT: >>>
This test case verifies that appropriate alerts are displayed to the user when system conditions warrant notification. It validates the alert presentation and timing.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. log in to the External application. 

2. Navigate to the Safety Checks tab in the Quality Assurance view. 

3. Check all toggles ( toggle to green option) except for the door interlock and Save Quality checks. 

4. Navigate back to the treatment view. 

5. Press the Prepare button.
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
5 - An alert message pops up, advising the user that the treatment is not enabled if the daily safety checks are not completed.
<<<

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H10TG-152
TITLE: Treatment View - Load a Treatment Plan
STATEMENT: >>>
This test case verifies the loading of treatment plans into the system. It validates that all plan parameters are correctly loaded and displayed.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Log in to the External application. 

2. Navigate to the treatment view. 

3. Validate the plan parameters against the plan in the internal application. 

4. Press Prepre 

5. Press Beam-on
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
4 - Verify that energy in the telemetry panel is ramping up to the energy of the plan. 

5 - Verify that when emission is completed, the timer has reached the plan’s duration
<<<

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H10TG-285
TITLE: Quality Assurance - Audit users' actions
STATEMENT: >>>
This test case verifies that system actions are properly logged and audited. It validates that the audit trail accurately records user actions and data modifications.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Log in to the External application. 

2. Navigate to the Beam QA Checks tab in the Quality Assurance view. 

3. Select Energy 50/70/100 in the Energy drop-down. 

4. Press prepare 

5. Press Beam-On to Start QC
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
3 - The action of QualityCheck triggered by the user is logged.
<<<

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H10TG-116
TITLE: Treatment View - Error Handling Received From Record and verify (DB)
STATEMENT: >>>
This test case verifies proper error handling and reporting. It validates that appropriate error messages are displayed and logged when system errors occur.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Log in to the External application. 

2. Navigate to the treatment view. 

3. Press the Prepare button to prepare the treatment. 

4. Press the Beam-On button to trigger emission delivery. 

5. Stop the Record and Verify docker in the internal system during the emission. 

6. Go to Log view.
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
6 - An error about the DB communication lost during emission should be displayed in the log list.
<<<

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H10TG-80
TITLE: Warm-Up - Log Performed Warm Up - Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
This test case verifies the system warmup and initialization process. It validates that the system is properly prepared for operation and all parameters are initialized.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Launch Heracles SW External. (The external unit should be located outside the treatment room). 

2. Click the Prepare button. 

3. Click the Reset button 

4. Click the QC tab 

5. Click the Daily Warm-Up tab 

1. Go to Log tab
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. There shall be a log of all (Full and Fast) warm-ups performed during the system's lifetime. 

Test being executed 

TC-H10TG-80-#14 

Warm-Up - Log Performed 
Warm Up - Test Case 

13.
<<<

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H10TG-65
TITLE: Treatment Console - Telemetry - (System status) - Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
This test case verifies system status and monitoring capabilities. It validates that system state information is accurately displayed and updated.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Log in to the External application. 

2. Navigate to the treatment view. 

3. Press the Prepare button to prepare the treatment. 

4. Press the Beam-On button to trigger emission delivery.
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1 - The interface should display the following states: 

System status: COLD 

3 - The interface should display the following steps: 

System status: WARMUP 

then System status: HVSetup ( On Loading) 

Upon completion of the preparation process: 

System status: READY 

4 - The interface should display the following steps: 

System status: Emission 

Upon completion of the process: 

System status: Primed
<<<

