[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H10TG-135
TITLE: Quality Assurance - Perform Quality Checks - Deviation
STATEMENT: >>>
This test case verifies quality assurance checks and validations. It ensures that the system properly executes quality control procedures.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Log in to the External application. 

2. Navigate to the Beam QA Checks tab in the Quality Assurance view. 

3. Select Energy 50/70/100 in the Energy drop-down. 

4. Press prepare 

5. Press Beam-On to Start QC 

6. Toggle to report view 

7. Select Applicator Size and Energy Level as performed in previous steps. 

8. Select reference QC result ( The reference is marked with [ref] label in the performed dropdown) 

9. Observe Intensity results 

10. Select the Last QC result (The last QC is the first item in the Performed dropdown) 

11. Observe the Intensity result. 

12. Select Deviation 

13. Observe the Intensity deviation result. 

14. Calculate the deviation of the last result from the reference result.
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>

14 - The table shows the deviation from the intensities of the reference QC for the selected Applicator, Energy level.
<<<

