[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H10TG-288
TITLE: Prevent Treatment Initiation for Unapproved Failed QC Tests
STATEMENT: >>>
This test case verifies that the system properly prevents or restricts certain operations. It validates that access control and business logic constraints are correctly enforced.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Log in to the External application. 

2. Navigate to the treatment view. 

3. Press the Prepare button to prepare the treatment. 

4. Log in to the Internal application. 

5. Navigate to the Quality Assurance view. 

6. Approve the latest QC test. 

7. Log in to the External application. 

8. Navigate to the treatment view. 

9. Press the Prepare button to prepare the treatment.
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
3 - An error message appears, alerting the user that the treatment cannot be delivered because the most recent QC test failed. 

9 - After approving the QC test, the prepare button is successfully triggered and the treatment can be delivered.
<<<

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H10TG-103
TITLE: Quality Assurance - Daily Warmup - Clear Errors - (UI) Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
This test case aims to verify that the application provides a control that allows the user to clear latched fault flags that occurred during the daily (Full) Warmup process.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
Intentionally create Daily Warmup errors in the system prior to conducting this test
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1.Launch Heracles External 

2.Click the Quality Assurance tab 

3.Inside the Quality Assurance tab, click the Daily Warmup tab 

4.Click the the Clear Error button
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
It should Clear latched fault flags that occurred during the daily (Full) Warmup process. 

This capability will allow the application to reset fault conditions after the fault is addressed or reviewed.
<<<

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H10TG-296
TITLE: Resume Uncompleted Treatment
STATEMENT: >>>
This test case verifies that the application enables the operator to resume an uncompleted treatment.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
Load a plan for treatment in the Heracles Internal unit.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Log in to the External application. 

2. Navigate to the treatment view. 

3. Press the Prepare button to prepare the treatment. 

4. Press the Beam-On button to trigger emission delivery. 

5. Press the stop button 

6. Unload the plan 

7. Log in to the Internal application. 

8. Navigate to the treatment view. 

9. Load the plan into the external application. 

10. Go to the External application. 

11. Press the Prepare button to prepare the treatment. 

12. Press Beam on.
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
The emission process should be stopped, and the status should become primed. 

6 - The plan should be unloaded and removed from the UI. 

11 - An alert message should be displayed informing the user that the treatment was not delivered completely and it will resume the 
emission for the remaining time. 

12 - The emission should run for the remining time.
<<<

